192.168.197.2>ntp

NAME
     ntp - query NTP servers state or update the local time via (S)NTP. 

SYNOPSIS
     ntp [-v] [-p] [-d] [-q] [-u] [-t timeout] [server] 

DESCRIPTION
     ntp queries the NTP servers about current state via the recommended NTP 
     control message. It can also query the NTP servers's time and update 
     the local time. 

     -v      Show ipntp product version.
     -p      queries NTP servers with the recommended NTP mode 6 control message 
             format about current state.
     -d      queries NTP servers with the recommended NTP mode 7 control message 
             format about current state.
     -q      query time from specified NTP server. 
     -u      read time from specified NTP server and update local time. 
     -t timeout
             Specifies the maximum time (in seconds) to wait for an answer from the (S)NTP
             server. A timeout value of -1 means that the program will wait forever.
             Default is 3 seconds.

RETURN VALUES
     The ntp command will exit with 0 on success, and non-zero on errors.

